================================================================================
                           DATA RELATIONSHIPS
================================================================================

DIAGRAM:

    ┌──────────┐         ┌──────────┐         ┌──────────────────┐
    │  USERS   │         │  ORDERS  │         │  MENU (items)    │
    └────┬─────┘         └────┬─────┘         └────────┬─────────┘
         │                    │                         │
         │ 1                  │ N                       │
         │                    │                         │
         │ places             │ contains                │ referenced_in
         │                    │                         │
         └────────────────────┘                         │
                       (via customerName field)          │
                                                        │
                                                        ▼
                                               ┌──────────────────┐
                                               │ Array in ORDER:  │
                                               │ {id, itemName,   │
                                               │  price}          │
                                               └──────────────────┘


RELATIONSHIP DETAILS:

1. USER → ORDER (One-to-Many)
   - A user can place multiple orders
   - Each order is linked to one user via customerName field
   - The relationship is implicit (not enforced by Firebase)

2. ORDER → MENU_ITEM (via embedded array)
   - Each order contains an array of items
   - Each item in the array references a menu item (by id and itemName)
   - This is an embedded relationship (denormalized)


================================================================================
                        SYSTEM WORKFLOW / LOGIC
================================================================================

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           1. USER REGISTRATION                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Step 1: User submits registration form
           ↓
   Step 2: System creates new document in 'users' collection
           ↓
   Step 3: User receives unique user_id (document ID)

   Data Flow: UI → createUser() → users collection

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           2. MENU MANAGEMENT                               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Admin Actions:
   • Add new menu item → addMenuItem() → menu collection
   • Update availability → updateMenuItemAvailability() 
   • Delete menu item → deleteMenuItem()
   • View all items → getMenuItems() / subscribeToMenu()

   Customer View:
   • Browse available items → subscribeToMenu() (real-time)

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           3. ORDER CREATION                                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Step 1: Customer adds items to cart
           ↓
   Step 2: Customer submits order (checkout)
           ↓
   Step 3: System calculates total from items
           ↓
   Step 4: Create order document with:
           - status: "NEW"
           - items: array of {id, itemName, price}
           - total: calculated sum
           - createdAt: current timestamp
           ↓
   Step 5: Order added to 'orders' collection via createOrder()

   Data Flow: Cart → createOrder() → orders collection

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           4. ORDER STATUS UPDATES                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Status Flow:

   NEW ──────→ IN_PROGRESS ──────→ READY ──────→ COMPLETED
                    │                    │
                    │                    └────────→ (for pickup)
                    │
                    └─────────────────────────────→ CANCELLED

   Kitchen Staff:
   • View new orders: subscribeToOrders()
   • Update status: updateOrderStatus(id, "IN_PROGRESS")
   • Mark ready: updateOrderStatus(id, "READY")
   
   Customer:
   • Track order: View order status in real-time

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           5. REAL-TIME UPDATES                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Firebase Features Used:
   • onSnapshot() - Real-time listeners for:
     - Menu items (availability changes)
     - Orders (new orders, status updates)
   
   This allows:
   - Kitchen to see new orders instantly
   - Customers to see order status changes in real-time
   - Admins to monitor all activity


